  <!--
    /stories, and the published-record detail pages beneath it.

    The detail route registered in App.tsx is /stories/:slug. Its URLs are DATA,
    not routes: one exists per published Case Study, they appear when a record is
    published and disappear when it is unpublished (spec section 35), and nothing
    in this repository generates this file - it is a static asset copied into the
    nginx image at build time.

    So there are three ways to include them, and only one of them is safe today:
      1. hardcode today's slugs here. Rejected. Spec section 28 forbids putting
         fixtures in the production sitemap, and any hand-written list starts
         rotting at the next publish or unpublish - a sitemap pointing at
         withdrawn records is worse than one that omits them, because it asks a
         crawler to index pages that answer "not found";
      2. serve a generated sitemap from the backend. That is a backend route and
         a deploy-time concern, deliberately out of scope for this task;
      3. let the index carry them. Chosen. /stories links every published record
         with a real anchor, and it is listed here with a monthly changefreq, so
         a crawler reaches every detail page in one hop from a URL that cannot
         go stale. Unpublished records are simply not linked, which is the same
         answer their own pages give.

    Option 2 stays the upgrade path if a sitemap-completeness need ever appears.
  -->
  <url>
    <loc>https://enterprise.colaberry.ai/stories</loc>
    <changefreq>monthly</changefreq>
    <priority>0.7</priority>
  </url>
